WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.507
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.507 --> 00:00:05.083
Today's message is, follow your dreams.

00:00:05.083 --> 00:00:06.542
Over to you, Chris Tucker.

00:00:06.542 --> 00:00:08.256
(rooster crows)

00:00:08.256 --> 00:00:11.607
(hip hop music)
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.607 --> 00:00:14.162
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:14.162 --> 00:00:18.306
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.306 --> 00:00:20.199
All that stuff I was just dreaming about,

00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:22.500
this is the possibilities that can happen

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.785
if I move to California, or if you know.

00:00:24.785 --> 00:00:26.105
Because I was working really hard here.

00:00:26.105 --> 00:00:28.244
A lot of comedians come
down from LA and say,

00:00:28.244 --> 00:00:31.240
"Man, you need to go to California,
'cause you pretty good."

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.283
I was getting a lot of good
advice, and a lot of people

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:34.688
who was really rooting for me.

00:00:34.688 --> 00:00:36.859
Yeah, I just went and
did it, but I had a dream

00:00:36.859 --> 00:00:41.279
and that dream gave me
confidence to keep going.

00:00:41.279 --> 00:00:44.681
The power of believing
and dreaming is real.

00:00:44.681 --> 00:00:48.598
Because that's all I did,
was dream and believe

00:00:48.598 --> 00:00:51.807
that these things could happen,
and it make me feel good.

00:00:51.807 --> 00:00:53.781
And that was my, that's true wealth.

00:00:53.781 --> 00:00:56.242
If you believe, and
you're doing something.

00:00:56.242 --> 00:00:58.784
You have a goal, you have
a dream to get somewhere.

00:00:58.784 --> 00:01:00.140
It makes you feel good.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.638
- This is something I think
is really, really, really

00:01:02.638 --> 00:01:05.973
important for especially
entrepreneurs to understand.

00:01:05.973 --> 00:01:09.577
In order for you to go out
and accomplish your dreams,

00:01:09.577 --> 00:01:12.679
you're going to have to do some
things that will scare you.

00:01:12.679 --> 00:01:15.105
You're going to have to push
outside your comfort zone.

00:01:15.105 --> 00:01:17.323
You're going to be put
in pressure situations

00:01:17.323 --> 00:01:18.762
that you've never been in before

00:01:18.762 --> 00:01:20.527
and you're going to want to shrink back.

00:01:20.527 --> 00:01:21.630
You're going to want to go down.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.929
You're going to want to
retreat inside and say, "No."

00:01:23.929 --> 00:01:25.485
To say, "I'm not ready, I'm not worthy.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:27.458
"I can't do that. That's not me.

00:01:27.458 --> 00:01:28.526
"I didn't go to school for that.

00:01:28.526 --> 00:01:29.513
"I don't know how to do that.

00:01:29.513 --> 00:01:31.557
"I've been told all my
life that I'm not able,

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:33.281
"I'm not capable. I don't
have the education."

00:01:33.281 --> 00:01:34.470
On and on and on and on.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.437
You'll find every logical
reason in the world

00:01:36.437 --> 00:01:38.949
why you can't go out
and do that big thing.

00:01:38.949 --> 00:01:41.897
You're going to come across multiple forks

00:01:41.897 --> 00:01:45.880
in the road along your
journey, multiple milestones.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.708
And you're going to want to shrink down.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:52.644
And the thing that gives you
the courage to keep going,

00:01:52.644 --> 00:01:56.811
to push through, to do that
scary thing, is your dream.

00:01:58.042 --> 00:02:00.373
The thing that allows you to push through

00:02:00.373 --> 00:02:04.290
all that craziness, all
that pain, awkwardness,

00:02:05.295 --> 00:02:08.616
uncomfortableness, is the big picture.

00:02:08.616 --> 00:02:10.380
Is what you want to go out and accomplish.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.759
And that's why it's so
important that you have a dream

00:02:13.759 --> 00:02:15.593
that really means something to you.

00:02:15.593 --> 00:02:17.521
I look at what I've done with my

00:02:17.521 --> 00:02:19.332
YouTube channel and helping entrepreneurs.

00:02:19.332 --> 00:02:22.095
And I used to self sabotage, a lot.

00:02:22.095 --> 00:02:23.813
I used to get speaking opportunities

00:02:23.813 --> 00:02:28.591
and give myself a reason that
I can't go out and do that.

00:02:28.591 --> 00:02:31.499
And I would say, "Oh, you know
my schedule's really busy."

00:02:31.499 --> 00:02:33.633
Come up with some excuse, when really

00:02:33.633 --> 00:02:35.365
I was just too afraid to do it.

00:02:35.365 --> 00:02:37.371
I was too afraid to be on stage and

00:02:37.371 --> 00:02:39.391
have thousands of people in the audience.

00:02:39.391 --> 00:02:41.375
And have it on national television.

00:02:41.375 --> 00:02:44.450
And have important people in
the room. I was too afraid.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:45.529
And I would secretly hope that

00:02:45.529 --> 00:02:47.538
people would cancel on me constantly.

00:02:47.538 --> 00:02:51.071
And it's the dream of what I want to do.

00:02:51.071 --> 00:02:53.935
It's the mission of helping
a billion entrepreneurs.

00:02:53.935 --> 00:02:57.964
It allows me to do the
things that I'm scared to do.

00:02:57.964 --> 00:03:00.599
It gives me the courage
to push through the pain,

00:03:00.599 --> 00:03:04.500
and the fear, and the
uncomfortableness, to try.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.764
If you want to do something big,

00:03:06.764 --> 00:03:08.691
if you want to have an impact,

00:03:08.691 --> 00:03:11.652
if you want to touch a
lot of people's lives,

00:03:11.652 --> 00:03:15.878
you can't do it being the
person that you are right now.

00:03:15.878 --> 00:03:17.886
You're going to have to grow.

00:03:17.886 --> 00:03:19.779
You're going to have to build muscles that

00:03:19.779 --> 00:03:21.462
you didn't know existed before.

00:03:21.462 --> 00:03:23.420
You're going to have to test yourself.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:24.829
It's going to happen.

00:03:24.829 --> 00:03:26.405
There will be so many times

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:29.713
along your journey that
you will be tested.

00:03:29.713 --> 00:03:32.302
And you will need to summon the courage

00:03:32.302 --> 00:03:35.664
inside of yourself to push through.

00:03:35.664 --> 00:03:40.155
And it comes from having
that big, bold dream

00:03:40.155 --> 00:03:41.773
that you want to go and make

00:03:41.773 --> 00:03:45.372
a big, important difference in the world.

00:03:45.372 --> 00:03:47.717
And so the next time you're faced with

00:03:47.717 --> 00:03:49.969
one of those uncomfortable challenges,

00:03:49.969 --> 00:03:54.323
when you're being called to the
task, I hope you'll say yes.

00:03:54.323 --> 00:03:58.874
I hope you'll follow your
dream, and not cow down.

00:03:58.874 --> 00:04:00.151
So the question of the day today is

00:04:00.151 --> 00:04:03.667
What was the hardest
thing you've had to do

00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:05.265
to stay on path with your dream?

00:04:05.265 --> 00:04:07.227
What's the biggest challenge,
the biggest obstacle

00:04:07.227 --> 00:04:09.735
you've had to face so far,
and how have your dreams

00:04:09.735 --> 00:04:11.291
helped you conquer it?

00:04:11.291 --> 00:04:13.102
I'm curious to find out,
and I think it can also

00:04:13.102 --> 00:04:15.633
serve as motivation for
other people watching.

00:04:15.633 --> 00:04:17.119
Please leave it down in the comments below

00:04:17.119 --> 00:04:19.307
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:04:19.307 --> 00:04:20.813
I also want to give a quick shout out to

00:04:20.813 --> 00:04:23.137
Tamyra Campbell, from Tam Cam Photo.

00:04:23.137 --> 00:04:25.888
Thank you so much for picking
up 10 copies of my book.

00:04:25.888 --> 00:04:27.043
It really, really, really means

00:04:27.043 --> 00:04:29.435
a lot to me, and I appreciate it.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.915
So, thank you guys again for watching.

00:04:30.915 --> 00:04:33.585
I believe in you, I hope
you continue to believe in

00:04:33.585 --> 00:04:36.534
yourself and whatever your one word is.

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:39.077
Much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:04:39.077 --> 00:04:41.338
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:04:41.338 --> 00:04:44.043
(hip hop music)
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:44.043 --> 00:04:47.711
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:04:47.711 --> 00:04:49.383
So as a special bonus for you guys

00:04:49.383 --> 00:04:51.752
to keep the energy high
on following your dreams,

00:04:51.752 --> 00:04:53.342
I'm going to share a couple extra clips

00:04:53.342 --> 00:04:54.852
that I hope you'll enjoy.

00:04:54.852 --> 00:04:56.616
- It's one of my favorite quotes.

00:04:56.616 --> 00:04:58.544
I came up with it, with my uncle

00:04:58.544 --> 00:05:01.009
I had a uncle named Uncle Shrimp

00:05:01.009 --> 00:05:02.183
- [Woman] Shrimp (laughs)

00:05:02.183 --> 00:05:05.253
- Uncle Shrimp, he was
a short kind of guy.

00:05:05.253 --> 00:05:08.760
Lost his hair at like the age
of 20, so he was bald-headed.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.256
And he was just so charismatic.

00:05:11.256 --> 00:05:13.607
And he told me this after I injured myself

00:05:13.607 --> 00:05:16.236
and I realized that I wasn't
going to be a football player.

00:05:16.236 --> 00:05:19.385
And he told me to never
lose sight of your dreams.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:23.086
But he also told me this, as who I was.

00:05:23.086 --> 00:05:26.581
He knew that now was going
to be a turning point.

00:05:26.581 --> 00:05:28.346
Either I could return to the streets,

00:05:28.346 --> 00:05:30.401
and follow in the footsteps of my father,

00:05:30.401 --> 00:05:32.484
or I could dream the impossible dream.

00:05:32.484 --> 00:05:33.675
- [Woman] Right

00:05:33.675 --> 00:05:37.390
- He also wanted me to notice,
as an African American man

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:41.307
because, you know, that
fear of having a dream,

00:05:42.201 --> 00:05:46.037
and that fear of, "Oh I can't dream that.

00:05:46.037 --> 00:05:48.838
"I'll never be able to do that."

00:05:48.838 --> 00:05:52.240
It was important to note that,
yes you can have that dream

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.829
but you have to know, honestly,
what it's going to take

00:05:54.829 --> 00:05:57.290
for you to achieve that dream.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.881
So then I came up with the quote

00:05:58.881 --> 00:06:01.957
and it goes for everybody,
all genders, all races.

00:06:01.957 --> 00:06:04.129
Don't be afraid to close
your eyes and dream,

00:06:04.129 --> 00:06:07.286
but then you have to open
your eyes and see the reality

00:06:07.286 --> 00:06:10.363
of what it's going to take
for you to achieve that dream.

00:06:10.363 --> 00:06:12.076
And a lot of people, they kind of see

00:06:12.076 --> 00:06:14.659
whether it's musicians, or
athletes, or entertainers

00:06:14.659 --> 00:06:16.342
or even just successful people.

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:19.744
But they don't understand the
thing that it takes for them

00:06:19.744 --> 00:06:23.500
to get to the point that they've gotten.

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.325
And that's why it's a very
important quote to me,

00:06:25.325 --> 00:06:28.104
and I think it has inspired people.

00:06:28.104 --> 00:06:30.447
And it inspires me every day.

00:06:30.447 --> 00:06:32.746
- Was playing the guitar your real dream?

00:06:32.746 --> 00:06:34.261
Your childhood dream?

00:06:34.261 --> 00:06:35.456
- I tell you, a funny dream, kind of.

00:06:35.456 --> 00:06:39.403
Because when I was about 11 years old,

00:06:39.403 --> 00:06:42.480
I was in, I think seventh grade.

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:44.732
From grade one to six
you're in this one school

00:06:44.732 --> 00:06:46.125
and then you go to this new school.

00:06:46.125 --> 00:06:49.596
And I went to this new school,
and there was this girl.

00:06:49.596 --> 00:06:52.459
This girl named Sandy.
She was so beautiful.

00:06:52.459 --> 00:06:53.640
(woman laughs)

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.440
Big blue eyes, and this
perfect heart-shaped face.

00:06:56.440 --> 00:07:01.282
And she was so, I was instantly
in love with this chick.

00:07:01.282 --> 00:07:03.383
So the first day, I asked her like,

00:07:03.383 --> 00:07:05.839
"You want to go steady with me?"

00:07:05.839 --> 00:07:09.063
(laughter)
She was like, "Okay."

00:07:09.063 --> 00:07:10.874
And so every day I'd
meet her at her locker,

00:07:10.874 --> 00:07:13.823
and we'd kiss at the locker
and then she'd get on her bus

00:07:13.823 --> 00:07:15.309
and I'd get on my bus and we'd go home

00:07:15.309 --> 00:07:17.561
and talk on the phone all night.

00:07:17.561 --> 00:07:21.061
And after seven days, she said, "You know,

00:07:23.399 --> 00:07:24.899
"I'm new here, and

00:07:28.559 --> 00:07:31.130
I just don't want to get tied down."

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.599
11 years old
(laughter)

00:07:33.599 --> 00:07:36.034
"I don't want to get tied
into a relationship."

00:07:36.034 --> 00:07:40.034
It absolutely broke my
heart. I was heartbroken.

00:07:41.921 --> 00:07:45.171
And that night, I had a dream

00:07:45.171 --> 00:07:47.679
that I was in a arena full of people

00:07:47.679 --> 00:07:51.534
and I was playing guitar,
and it was this packed arena

00:07:51.534 --> 00:07:53.298
and they're all going, "Yeah!"

00:07:53.298 --> 00:07:55.388
And I'm playing, and I look down

00:07:55.388 --> 00:07:59.561
and she's staring at me and
she's crying like (sobbing).

00:07:59.561 --> 00:08:02.579
(laughter and applause)

00:08:02.579 --> 00:08:04.496
That's true, and that--

00:08:05.444 --> 00:08:08.033
- Revenge
- [Dave] Yeah

00:08:08.033 --> 00:08:10.088
My rock and roll revenge
- [Host] We all--

00:08:10.088 --> 00:08:11.609
- You could have been my girlfriend.

00:08:11.609 --> 00:08:14.360
- We all have this dream,
but we just don't end up

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:16.380
in the Foo Fighters, that's the problem.

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:17.689
(laughter)
- Dreams come true.

00:08:17.689 --> 00:08:20.211
- It's hard changing your life.

00:08:20.211 --> 00:08:24.396
It was hard when just over three years ago

00:08:24.396 --> 00:08:27.566
in the Penobscot Building
in Detroit, Michigan,

00:08:27.566 --> 00:08:29.980
where I was operating my business

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:32.175
and I fell on some hard times

00:08:32.175 --> 00:08:35.623
and I was sleeping in my office.

00:08:35.623 --> 00:08:38.131
It was hard coming into the lobby,

00:08:38.131 --> 00:08:40.000
and the security says,
"Excuse me, Mr. Brown.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.637
"Can we see you for a moment?"

00:08:41.637 --> 00:08:44.179
And I said, "Yes," and I
walked up to the counter

00:08:44.179 --> 00:08:47.140
and he gave me an envelope, and he said,

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.731
"Would you mind reading it here?"

00:08:48.731 --> 00:08:50.948
And I opened the envelope,
and the envelope was

00:08:50.948 --> 00:08:55.914
from management that said,
"This is an office tower.

00:08:55.914 --> 00:09:00.081
"It's not a hotel. Please do
not sleep in your office."

00:09:02.513 --> 00:09:06.305
And I said, "Excuse me sir," I
said, "I just work long hours

00:09:06.305 --> 00:09:09.521
"in creating my business.
I'm an entrepreneur.

00:09:09.521 --> 00:09:11.854
"And right now things are bad for me.

00:09:11.854 --> 00:09:16.426
"But they're not going
to be this way always."

00:09:16.426 --> 00:09:18.574
And I just asked for the opportunity

00:09:18.574 --> 00:09:20.954
to continue to operate like I'm doing.

00:09:20.954 --> 00:09:23.775
I'm not trying to make this my home.

00:09:23.775 --> 00:09:26.167
And it was hard coming through the lobby.

00:09:26.167 --> 00:09:27.235
And sometimes they would laugh,

00:09:27.235 --> 00:09:29.371
there's the guy talking
about becoming successful

00:09:29.371 --> 00:09:33.353
and look at him, he's bathing
in the bathroom upstairs.

00:09:33.353 --> 00:09:37.266
On the 21st floor, he sleeps on the floor.

00:09:37.266 --> 00:09:41.410
Him and two other dreamers
up there, look at him.

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:43.291
It was hard, ladies and gentlemen,

00:09:43.291 --> 00:09:46.577
coming to speak to people and I was facing

00:09:46.577 --> 00:09:49.282
financial difficulties in my own life.

00:09:49.282 --> 00:09:51.372
I was behind on my bills and my dreams,

00:09:51.372 --> 00:09:54.646
and I'm saying to them,
"You can live your dream."

00:09:54.646 --> 00:09:56.747
It was hard, ladies and gentlemen.

00:09:56.747 --> 00:09:59.975
It was very difficult to
pick myself up each day

00:09:59.975 --> 00:10:01.832
believing that I could do it.

00:10:01.832 --> 00:10:03.887
There were times that I doubted myself.

00:10:03.887 --> 00:10:07.045
I said, "God, why is
this happening to me?"

00:10:07.045 --> 00:10:10.041
I'm just trying to take care
of my children and my mother.

00:10:10.041 --> 00:10:13.524
I'm not trying to steal
or rob from anybody.

00:10:13.524 --> 00:10:16.763
Why did this have to happen to me?

00:10:16.763 --> 00:10:21.558
It was very hard, and here's
what I want to say to you,

00:10:21.558 --> 00:10:25.122
for those of you that have
experienced some hardships,

00:10:25.122 --> 00:10:27.757
don't give up on your dream.

00:10:27.757 --> 00:10:31.357
No one could have
convinced me by holding on,

00:10:31.357 --> 00:10:33.980
by continuing to push forward,

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:37.475
by continuing to run toward my dream,

00:10:37.475 --> 00:10:41.058
that one day I would
have my own talk show.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:44.005
It's a long shot, ladies and gentlemen.

00:10:44.005 --> 00:10:47.488
From Liberty City, in an
abandoned building, on a floor,

00:10:47.488 --> 00:10:50.693
never knowing my mother or
father, it's a long shot.

00:10:50.693 --> 00:10:53.537
Being here with you today in this dome,

00:10:53.537 --> 00:10:55.917
in Atlanta, it's a long shot.

00:10:55.917 --> 00:10:58.866
No college training, labeled
educable mentally retarded.

00:10:58.866 --> 00:11:01.705
But I kept running toward my dream.

00:11:01.705 --> 00:11:04.872
(cheering from crowd)

00:11:08.851 --> 00:11:12.101
Don't stop.
(cheering)

00:11:15.748 --> 00:11:18.998
Don't stop.
(cheering)

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:34.010
Don't stop running towards your dream.

